Z||000002||SKIDMARK||10-13-2001||09:39 PM||||It all depends on how wet the pavement is. My 85 4 cyl with 175K peels real good in reverse. Won't even squeek in drive. I expect to break something soon.<P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||10
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||10-13-2001||09:44 PM||||Put in N. Rev to 5k rpm. Drop into D.<BR>You will do quite a burn out. But your transmission {might}/{probably will} explode. :-D<P>I was joking! Don't ever do what I said.<P>Four cylinder automatics will not burn out. Maybe around a corner or in rain. You need a stick to do much. I dont ever think V6 fiero with the auto can do much of a burn out. Plus the 3 speed slushbox kind of sucks.<P><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000004||Old Lar||10-13-2001||09:45 PM||||The 4 cylinder automatic was not meant to be a tire burning dragster.  The engine's weight is over the rear drive wheels which give you good traction.  Maybe if you spread some loose gravel under the tires, they may spin.  Do that a few times to get your jollies, then come back crying that you just sent a rod through engine of the 84.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gerald||10-13-2001||11:03 PM||||87 4 cyl 5 speed. When shes running right she will go sideways on demand. I need new coils now thou. Power loss  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> But the new clutch helps.<P>------------------<BR>87 coupe 5 spd||||reg||1
Z||000006||LivoniaFieroGT||10-13-2001||11:43 PM||||No need to continue thinking down those acceleration lines.  I've had a four and she purred nicely under full accel but not a squeek.  And my perfect running GT auto is no better.  Just accelerates faster.... but no squeal. Auto's just go.  It is the 5 speeds I've had that can really be fun!!    So enjoy and don't abuse...||||reg||9
Z||000007||BlackDragon||10-14-2001||12:23 AM||||step 1: place foot firmly on break pedal<BR>step 2: place car in drive<BR>step 3: push gas to the floor (note: do not release break)<BR>that always did it for me, but i dont know how it will do in a 4 cyl auto. do it too many times and a new transaxle will be needed, but on occasion it is not too rough on the car. <BR>note: these are personal oppinions and do not provide a warantee  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>We are all different for a reason.....<BR>you can read a persons soul through there eyes.....<BR>he who argues with a fool is probably one himself.....<BR>big cars may be fast, but i can corner.....<P>BlackDragonsEmail@yahoo.com||||reg||1
Z||000008||Kasdan||10-14-2001||12:59 AM||||will an 86 gt auto power brake very easily?  do both tires spin?||||reg||1
Z||000009||sloth85GT||10-14-2001||01:34 AM||||I can squeal my 85 GT but I can't lay rubber because the weight is right over the rear wheels that the car just hooks up really well. I can't imagine the 95HP Duke making anything more than a little sqeak with that kind of traction. If you're got a 4 speed, you're more likely to be able to squeak the rubber because it's got better gearing and you can just drop the clutch. <P>Note: I don't not recommend nor condone dropping the clutch. Do so at your own risk.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>[edit]I just noticed you have the auto, so the answer is, probably not to your question.[/edit]<BR>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">      <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<p>[This message has been edited by sloth85GT (edited 10-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||SLYGUY||10-14-2001||01:41 AM||||You have to really abuse an automatic to get the rear tires loose. An automatic with a four cylinder 90hp powerplant?<BR>Forget about it. Get the V6, with a manual. <P>I haven't tried it much. There isn't much to gain, and an awful lot to loose.<P>Pulled a mean broadie once on accident. A full 360. Don't remember if that was more fun or terrifying though!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000011||Standard||10-14-2001||02:15 AM||||Wanna peel out?  Get some 165/85 13's on there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Really wanna peel out?  Add 4 more cylinders  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">         <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
