Z||000018||Seanh||10-14-2001||01:25 PM||||I have an 86GT 3.4 w/TH125c tranny (yes, I changed it, I killed the OD on the old tranny and I like the gearing on this one better). The only ways I can get the car to really burn out is Neutral dropping, which is not reccomend, but I was getting rid of the tranny anyway. I must have done it atleast 20 times and it didn't appear to hurt the tranny anymore then it already was. Although, the motor bogs down quite a bit when you drop into drive and it gave me slower times, so it gains nothing really... Personally I love burning out, but this Fiero is a pain to do it in. One some pavementes I can get it to powerstall, but it has to be really slick to do it.  I think a huge reason it won't powerstall is the fact it has 4 wheel disk brakes too. Also, yes it does turn over both tires, so thats a contributing factor too. I am waiting to install a line locker on the front brake circut to lock the front wheels while leaving the back free. It was about $40 from JC Whitney and its kinda a replacment to a parking brake for brake conversions. I'm not going to use it for a parking brake, just using it to do burnouts before racing...<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 4spd Auto, getting ready to install T-6 turbo.||||reg||1
