Z||000022||Tryxalon||10-14-2001||07:13 PM||||I admit to having read only a few posts before jumping in here to share my views. <P>One of the things I enjoy most about the Mid-engine design is the enhanced tendency to use physics most efficiently.  The concentric cemter of the of the powered engine/transmission rotation applied to the tangent of wheel-road interface tends to transmit the torque in a manner where the vehicular center of gravity enhances the friction neccesary for traction. <P>That means that the Fiero is designed NOT to waste energy in spinning the rear tires; the Fiero is designed to "nove on down the road!!" Of course, there is the possibility that you may enjoy sitting in one place!  <P>Myself, I prefer to enjoy my Fiero "in  actual motion", rather than "spinning my wheels"     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>(just a little ribbing! 84fierotrevor!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Tryxalon (edited 10-14-2001).]||||reg||1
